.md
## Frontend support for string operators
We extended the tiny WL interpreter that runs on the frontend with more string-related operators, such as `ToString`, `NumberForm`, `StringJoin`, and `Round`. Can you guess the use case?

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
## Frontend support for string operators
We extended the tiny WL interpreter that runs on the frontend with more string-related operators, such as `ToString`, `NumberForm`, `StringJoin`, and `Round`. Can you guess the use case?

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
sqval = 0.3;
EventHandler[InputRange[0.33,1,0.1], (sqval=(*SqB[*)Sqrt[#](*]SqB*))&]

TextView[
  sqval // Offload,
  "Label" -> "Before"
]

TextView[
  StringJoin["sqval = ", 
    ToString[NumberForm[sqval, {4,2}]
  ]] // Offload,
  "Label" -> "After"
]

