%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
## Improved support for packed arrays
We improved how packed arrays are stored and copied from the Wolfram Kernel to the frontend. Usually, during initial evaluation, any `Graphics` or `Image` expression is serialized as `"ExpressionJSON"` and then reinterpreted on the frontend, while subsequent updates use the binary WXF format. However, this initial evaluation is still very inefficient, because by default any numeric or packed array is serialized as a plain list, making the payload 10-100 times larger. We patched the standard JSON serializer to ship any packed or numeric array as a base64-encoded string using WXF as a container. This is especially important for data structures such as `Image` and `Graphics3D` with many vertices.

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
## Improved support for packed arrays
We improved how packed arrays are stored and copied from the Wolfram Kernel to the frontend. Usually, during initial evaluation, any `Graphics` or `Image` expression is serialized as `"ExpressionJSON"` and then reinterpreted on the frontend, while subsequent updates use the binary WXF format. However, this initial evaluation is still very inefficient, because by default any numeric or packed array is serialized as a plain list, making the payload 10-100 times larger. We patched the standard JSON serializer to ship any packed or numeric array as a base64-encoded string using WXF as a container. This is especially important for data structures such as `Image` and `Graphics3D` with many vertices.

